WEBVTT

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:01.118
Previously on The O. C:

00:00:01.327 --> 00:00:02.911
Know what I like about rich kids?

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.830
- Nothing.
- Let me meet you upstairs.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.039
- Summer?
- Anna?

00:00:06.248 --> 00:00:07.874
- Seth?
- The gruesome twosome.

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:10.918
You spent the weekend painting
Jimmy's house, and I didn't say a word...

00:00:11.127 --> 00:00:13.504
...because I knew nothing was going on.
- Of course.

00:00:47.657 --> 00:00:48.866
Do I have a fever?

00:00:49.075 --> 00:00:51.494
I think I might have a fever
and/or the chills.

00:00:51.702 --> 00:00:54.788
- Since when?
- Since recently.

00:00:54.996 --> 00:00:57.499
So you're not feeling well?

00:00:57.707 --> 00:00:59.876
No, I feel fine.

00:01:00.543 --> 00:01:03.712
Just my head's a little achy
and my stomach's kind of weird. I'm okay.

00:01:03.921 --> 00:01:05.213
Come here.

00:01:08.132 --> 00:01:10.885
- You don't feel warm.
- What about cold or clammy?

00:01:11.052 --> 00:01:15.347
- Maybe you've got the summer flu.
- Yeah. It's November, but it's possible.

00:01:15.555 --> 00:01:17.640
Maybe you need some Anna-biotics.

00:01:19.809 --> 00:01:24.313
- Do you not want to go to school?
- No, Dad. I want to go to school. Okay?

00:01:25.313 --> 00:01:27.816
- I'm just worried about infecting others.
- You're right.

00:01:28.024 --> 00:01:30.860
We should just take you
straight to the emergency room.

00:01:31.027 --> 00:01:32.027
Just to be sure.

00:01:32.236 --> 00:01:37.198
Okay. Or I could stay home
and try and sleep it off.

00:01:37.407 --> 00:01:40.826
Or you could go to school,
face Summer and Anna and apologize.

00:01:41.035 --> 00:01:44.246
First of all, no.
Second of all, no.

00:01:44.454 --> 00:01:46.122
Why would I?

00:01:46.331 --> 00:01:49.208
Oh, the Summer flu.

00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:52.503
I just got it. That was good.

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:55.714
It's not my fault that they both
tried to kiss me on Thanksgiving.

00:01:55.922 --> 00:01:57.715
What was I supposed to do?
Not kiss back?

00:01:57.924 --> 00:01:59.884
Say "No, stop"?
Risk hurting their feelings?

00:02:00.092 --> 00:02:02.678
Well, it seems you already did
hurt their feelings.

00:02:02.886 --> 00:02:05.806
Yeah, perhaps I did,
but what about my feelings, okay?

00:02:06.014 --> 00:02:08.141
I was the one who was assaulted.
I'm the victim.

00:02:08.349 --> 00:02:10.893
Hey, how come you're not dressed?
You're gonna be late.

00:02:11.102 --> 00:02:14.771
And so are you. Or is that what ladies
are wearing these days to Yogalates?

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.691
Taryn called to remind you that today is
the first day of your Yogalates workshop.

00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:23.821
- Okay. Mom, Yogalates?
- I don't know if I'm gonna go.

00:02:24.029 --> 00:02:26.156
- I'm not feeling well.
- See? It's contagious.

00:02:26.364 --> 00:02:28.950
You know, honey, you might
still be a little hung-over.

00:02:29.158 --> 00:02:30.159
From what?

00:02:30.368 --> 00:02:32.870
I don't know. Getting drunk
and passing out on Thanksgiving?

00:02:33.078 --> 00:02:36.206
Hey, I had two glasses of wine.

00:02:36.414 --> 00:02:37.790
Three.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.334
I'm sure Julie Cooper
has spread word around town...

00:02:40.543 --> 00:02:42.253
...that I now have a drinking problem.

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.379
Which is why you
have to go to Yogalates.

00:02:44.588 --> 00:02:48.591
Because you know those chatty Newpsies
will assume you're sleeping off a bender.

00:02:48.758 --> 00:02:51.302
And Summer and Anna
will assume you're afraid of them.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.680
Hey, I'm not afraid of Summer
and Anna, all right?

00:02:54.888 --> 00:02:57.557
- Well, I'm not afraid of Anna.
- So you're going to school.

00:02:57.724 --> 00:02:59.851
- And you're going to Yogalates.
- You like saying that.

00:03:00.059 --> 00:03:02.353
Yogalates? I kind of do.

00:03:02.561 --> 00:03:04.146
- Yogalates.
- Yogalates.

00:03:04.354 --> 00:03:07.982
You know what I want to know,
is why these two are so smug.

00:03:08.191 --> 00:03:10.651
Because for once,
they didn't do anything wrong?

00:03:11.152 --> 00:03:12.611
That's true.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:16.156
- Here's to you.
- Back at you.

00:03:16.656 --> 00:03:19.659
Enjoy it, boys,
because knowing the two of you...

00:03:19.867 --> 00:03:21.744
...it won't last long.
- Yogalates.

00:03:52.811 --> 00:03:57.398
Your class presentations will account
for one-third of your final grade...

00:03:57.607 --> 00:04:01.819
...along with your term papers
and, of course, the final exam.

00:04:01.986 --> 00:04:04.988
I'll be dividing the class
into two-person teams.

00:04:05.197 --> 00:04:09.200
Each team will be responsible
for presenting a detailed account...

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:13.912
...of a pivotal event or period
in European history.

00:04:14.121 --> 00:04:16.539
I've already had quite a few
partnership requests...

00:04:17.999 --> 00:04:20.251
...however,
in fairness to the other students...

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:23.295
...I will select the teams myself
at random.

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:26.131
Lauren and Kenny,
the French Revolution.

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:31.635
Ryan and Luke,
the Spanish Inquisition.

00:04:31.844 --> 00:04:35.013
Stephanie and Bobby,
the Protestant Reformation.

00:04:35.222 --> 00:04:37.057
Stephanie? Are you listening?

00:04:37.265 --> 00:04:39.100
Stephanie? Miss Savage, please.

00:04:39.308 --> 00:04:41.602
- You and Luke?
- I know.

00:04:41.811 --> 00:04:43.479
Holy unholy alliances.

00:04:43.687 --> 00:04:46.690
This is why I asked Mr. Bendis
a week ago if we could be partners.

00:04:46.898 --> 00:04:49.734
- To avoid a situation like this.
- Why? Who did you get?

00:04:49.942 --> 00:04:52.778
Marcy Ross and I
are doing Cort Ás and the Aztecs.

00:04:52.986 --> 00:04:56.781
I like Marcy Ross. She's got a good smile
on her. It's innocent but it's knowing.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:00.117
- You're going after Marcy now too?
- Hey. I'm the victim here, okay?

00:05:00.326 --> 00:05:03.287
Don't tell me, tell Summer and Anna.

00:05:03.495 --> 00:05:06.248
And, hey, eventually you might
want to tell Marcy too.

00:05:06.915 --> 00:05:09.959
What are you and Luke doing?
That was me ignoring you, by the way.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:12.586
Spanish Inquisition.
Meeting at his house after school.

00:05:12.795 --> 00:05:15.338
You're going into the belly of the beast?

00:05:15.547 --> 00:05:19.217
Hey, it's not gonna be that bad. Who
knows, you might end up being friends.

00:05:20.426 --> 00:05:22.594
- You think?
- No, it's too weird.

00:05:22.803 --> 00:05:25.222
I mean, my ex-boyfriend
hanging out with my boyfriend?

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:28.891
- What are you guys gonna talk about?
- I can only think of one thing.

00:05:30.768 --> 00:05:33.479
So I talked to my guy at the SEC
and your clients...

00:05:33.687 --> 00:05:38.107
...and they all agree that if you make
full restitution by January 1 st...

00:05:38.316 --> 00:05:41.777
- But that means selling the house.
- And avoiding criminal prosecution.

00:05:41.986 --> 00:05:44.154
- And jail time.
- I can't sell the house now...

00:05:44.363 --> 00:05:47.782
...it's almost the holidays.
I can't do that to Julie and Kaitlin.

00:05:47.991 --> 00:05:50.910
They wouldn't have to move out
right away. Just show the house...

00:05:51.118 --> 00:05:52.953
...when Julie and Kaitlin are out.

00:05:53.162 --> 00:05:56.289
What if she says no? She's on
the title too. What if she won't sell?

00:05:56.498 --> 00:06:00.835
What choice does she have? She can't
afford to live there if you're in jail.

00:06:01.043 --> 00:06:04.171
Now that she's got
Caleb Nichol in her pocket...

00:06:04.379 --> 00:06:07.465
- You had lunch with him?
- No.

00:06:07.674 --> 00:06:11.302
I had lunch with Ryan.
Seth was just, you know, there.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:15.263
I cannot believe you.
Coop, where is your loyalty?

00:06:15.472 --> 00:06:17.098
- What did he say?
- Nothing.

00:06:17.307 --> 00:06:20.142
- I'm not getting involved.
- That means he said something.

00:06:20.309 --> 00:06:24.021
- What did he say?
- Nothing. I told you.

00:06:24.229 --> 00:06:25.480
Hey.

00:06:25.689 --> 00:06:28.441
Hello. What did he say?

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:31.986
- What did who say?
- Seth.

00:06:32.194 --> 00:06:34.946
Oh, it's you.

00:06:40.201 --> 00:06:43.287
You're, like, flossing.
At school.

00:06:45.163 --> 00:06:49.375
Do you have any idea how much bacteria
accumulates between lunch and dinner?

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:52.878
No. But the fact that you do
tells me everything.

00:06:54.671 --> 00:06:57.757
Look, if you want him,
you can have him. I'm done.

00:06:58.174 --> 00:07:00.926
Thanks. But that's okay.

00:07:01.135 --> 00:07:03.679
Right. Because you couldn't
be interested in someone...

00:07:03.887 --> 00:07:06.139
...that's interested in me.

00:07:06.348 --> 00:07:09.559
No. Because I couldn't possibly
be interested in someone...

00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:12.311
...who treats women that way.

00:07:18.107 --> 00:07:20.943
So how much bacteria? Like, a lot?

00:07:22.319 --> 00:07:23.946
A lot.

00:07:24.821 --> 00:07:25.989
Thanks.

00:07:31.744 --> 00:07:34.329
Hey, I was hoping I'd bump into you.
I wanted to...

00:07:34.538 --> 00:07:35.747
Hi, Summer.

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:40.876
And Anna hanging out together.

00:07:41.502 --> 00:07:43.795
That's... That's awkward.

00:07:44.004 --> 00:07:46.506
- Not really.
- Well, I meant for me.

00:07:46.715 --> 00:07:50.301
How are you guys?
You guys good? You guys getting along?

00:07:50.509 --> 00:07:54.554
Yes. In fact, we were just about
to go to the library...

00:07:54.721 --> 00:07:56.431
...to do some research.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.099
We were?

00:07:58.266 --> 00:08:00.142
Yeah. The library.

00:08:00.726 --> 00:08:02.728
- For books.
- Books.

00:08:02.936 --> 00:08:06.439
Yeah. And then we thought we'd go
shopping, right? South Coast Plaza?

00:08:06.648 --> 00:08:08.608
- Sounds good. Okay.
- All right.

00:08:08.816 --> 00:08:10.443
Okay.

00:08:12.653 --> 00:08:14.946
That doesn't sound good at all.

00:08:20.743 --> 00:08:24.788
- Hey, guys.
- Kirsten. You made it.

00:08:24.955 --> 00:08:26.956
How are you feeling, sweetie?

00:08:27.165 --> 00:08:30.584
Julie told us you were
"under the weather" at Thanksgiving.

00:08:30.793 --> 00:08:35.130
- She did?
- Oh, well, the holidays can be so stressful.

00:08:35.338 --> 00:08:39.008
I could go for a little hair of the dog
myself right about now.

00:08:39.217 --> 00:08:41.177
We'll see you out there.

00:08:41.385 --> 00:08:43.929
- Hey, wait up, guys.
- Julie.

00:08:44.137 --> 00:08:46.556
Kirsten, you showed up.
How are you feeling?

00:08:46.765 --> 00:08:49.600
So did you tell everyone
I was drunk at Thanksgiving?

00:08:49.809 --> 00:08:52.061
Everyone was wondering
where you were, so...

00:08:52.269 --> 00:08:54.313
I was at the office working.

00:08:54.521 --> 00:08:56.564
Well, hey, it's okay.
We're all friends here.

00:08:56.773 --> 00:08:59.859
If we're all friends,
why don't you start acting like one?

00:09:07.532 --> 00:09:09.617
- Hi. Ryan, isn't it?
- Hi.

00:09:09.826 --> 00:09:11.744
Luke will be right down. Come in.

00:09:11.952 --> 00:09:14.496
- No! Mine!
- Give me! Give it!

00:09:14.705 --> 00:09:16.081
- Stop! The head!
- Just give...

00:09:16.248 --> 00:09:19.167
- Stop it.
- Guys, guys. This is Luke's friend Ryan.

00:09:19.375 --> 00:09:21.252
Ryan, this is Eric and Brad.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.003
- Give it now.
- Stop.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:24.713
- Who wants a snack?
- Me.

00:09:24.921 --> 00:09:26.673
Ryan?

00:09:26.881 --> 00:09:29.258
- Hello.
- Daddy, you're home.

00:09:30.009 --> 00:09:33.095
- There they are. How are you doing?
- Can we play some ball later?

00:09:33.303 --> 00:09:36.556
You know what, kids,
I'm just home to drop off Mom's car.

00:09:36.765 --> 00:09:41.102
One of the belts was misaligned. I had
them change the oil too. Sorry, fellas.

00:09:41.977 --> 00:09:45.188
You remember Luke's friend Ryan.
They're doing a project together.

00:09:45.397 --> 00:09:48.066
- Yeah? What about?
- Spanish Inquisition.

00:09:48.274 --> 00:09:50.651
Not one of Western civilization's
proudest moments.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:54.655
I was a history major at USC.
Now I sell cars for a living.

00:09:54.863 --> 00:09:57.323
Don't listen to him, Ryan.
He owns three dealerships.

00:09:57.532 --> 00:10:00.993
- God, Mom. Brag much?
- She's just being proud of me.

00:10:01.202 --> 00:10:03.203
Let's just do this.
We got a lot of work.

00:10:03.412 --> 00:10:05.914
Yeah, me too. Gus is outside.
I'll see you tonight.

00:10:06.122 --> 00:10:08.333
Ryan, keep him on his toes, please.

00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:10.418
Luke, SC-Notre Dame this Saturday.

00:10:10.626 --> 00:10:12.961
Thought we'd drive up about noon.
Tailgate.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.379
Yeah, cool.

00:10:14.588 --> 00:10:17.549
Ryan, it's gonna be a good game.
You're more than welcome.

00:10:17.757 --> 00:10:21.469
- Come on, give it back. It's not yours!
- Guys!

00:10:26.056 --> 00:10:28.516
So how you wanna do this?

00:10:29.767 --> 00:10:31.143
I don't know. I was thinking...

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.563
Because I got books from the library,
I pulled some stuff off the Web.

00:10:34.771 --> 00:10:37.941
I was thinking we could do, like,
a screen show on my PowerBook.

00:10:38.149 --> 00:10:41.068
My dad's got a scanner at the office,
color LaserJet, PowerPoint.

00:10:41.277 --> 00:10:44.279
We could just pull some stuff here
and then head over there.

00:10:45.363 --> 00:10:46.823
You know, or not.

00:10:47.949 --> 00:10:50.076
No, no. That sounds good.

00:10:52.286 --> 00:10:53.287
Yeah.

00:10:57.999 --> 00:11:01.168
- Hello?
- Hey. It's me. Can you talk?

00:11:01.377 --> 00:11:04.588
Yeah. I'm just packing
some of Marissa's winter things.

00:11:04.796 --> 00:11:06.923
I'll drop them by in the morning,
if that's okay.

00:11:07.132 --> 00:11:09.217
Yeah. Yeah, that's great.

00:11:10.426 --> 00:11:14.012
- What's going on, Jimmy?
- Look, l... I had a meeting with Sandy.

00:11:14.221 --> 00:11:18.766
And it looks like I have to pay
everything back by January 1 st.

00:11:18.975 --> 00:11:22.353
- Jimmy, it's the holidays.
- I don't have any other choice.

00:11:22.561 --> 00:11:25.230
What are Kaitlin and I supposed to do?
Where will we live?

00:11:25.439 --> 00:11:27.774
Live with your mother or... Caleb's.

00:11:29.317 --> 00:11:33.570
No, we can't. And we shouldn't have to.
This is my house too. And Kaitlin's.

00:11:33.779 --> 00:11:36.865
- And we're not selling.
- Julie, I could go to jail.

00:11:38.533 --> 00:11:41.911
Maybe you should, Jimmy.
Have you ever thought about that?

00:11:42.244 --> 00:11:45.247
Maybe you deserve to go to jail.

00:11:48.916 --> 00:11:50.793
Dad?

00:11:52.586 --> 00:11:54.171
Hello?

00:11:54.379 --> 00:11:56.256
Dad, you here?

00:11:57.382 --> 00:12:00.051
I don't know. He must've gone home.

00:12:04.012 --> 00:12:06.931
Nice, huh? They're giving these away.

00:12:12.645 --> 00:12:13.854
Oh, nice. It's in.

00:12:14.062 --> 00:12:16.981
Check it out:
450 horsepower, 8-cylinder.

00:12:21.944 --> 00:12:24.529
Dude, you have to get in.

00:12:32.077 --> 00:12:33.454
Wow, man.

00:12:33.662 --> 00:12:36.122
The stereo's insane.

00:12:39.917 --> 00:12:41.627
Is that your dad?

00:12:43.003 --> 00:12:45.088
Yeah, and that's
his business partner, Gus.

00:12:45.297 --> 00:12:47.173
We should go say hey.

00:13:32.544 --> 00:13:34.421
- Lf you tell anyone...
- I won't.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.215
- Go! Let's go!
- Luke?

00:13:39.759 --> 00:13:41.469
Luke!

00:13:49.392 --> 00:13:52.770
Sorry I'm late.
I slept through my alarm.

00:13:52.978 --> 00:13:54.688
No, it's okay.

00:13:57.065 --> 00:14:00.109
How'd it go last night?
You didn't call me, so...

00:14:00.318 --> 00:14:04.196
- We were working pretty late.
- Did you meet his mom? She's really great.

00:14:04.404 --> 00:14:07.407
- Seemed nice, yeah.
- And I'm sure his dad was out of town?

00:14:07.615 --> 00:14:11.452
- No, he was there.
- Really? Because he's never around.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:15.497
He's got these dealerships in other cities,
and he's always traveling.

00:14:16.873 --> 00:14:18.166
What?

00:14:18.374 --> 00:14:20.835
Nothing. Just...

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.420
- I need some coffee.
- Okay.

00:14:23.629 --> 00:14:26.298
I knew you guys would talk.
So, what did he say about me?

00:14:27.007 --> 00:14:28.466
Nothing.

00:14:29.509 --> 00:14:31.427
Fine. I'll go grab Seth.

00:14:31.635 --> 00:14:33.012
Wait.

00:14:37.515 --> 00:14:39.976
Something happened last night.

00:14:40.726 --> 00:14:43.228
But I told Luke I wouldn't say anything.

00:14:43.437 --> 00:14:45.939
Is it...? Is he okay?

00:14:46.398 --> 00:14:47.774
What is it?

00:14:47.941 --> 00:14:50.026
Ryan, you can tell me.

00:14:50.234 --> 00:14:52.695
You can't tell anyone,
not even Summer.

00:14:52.903 --> 00:14:55.238
- Especially Summer.
- I won't. I swear.

00:14:55.447 --> 00:14:58.825
- Because I'm not even telling Seth.
- You can trust me.

00:14:59.033 --> 00:15:01.994
I won't say a word. I promise.

00:15:05.872 --> 00:15:09.000
Well, apparently some of us
are on Central time.

00:15:09.208 --> 00:15:10.960
Yeah, sorry.

00:15:12.878 --> 00:15:16.131
So how was your date with Luke,
your new study buddy?

00:15:16.339 --> 00:15:20.468
- It was fine. Something for the road?
- Yes, I'd like something. It's called gossip.

00:15:20.676 --> 00:15:23.554
Was there any cross-burning?
Any goose-stepping?

00:15:23.762 --> 00:15:25.639
Small Taiwanese family
locked in the basement?

00:15:25.847 --> 00:15:28.516
- Not so much. Fruit? Bagel?
- Yeah, a bagel would be good.

00:15:28.683 --> 00:15:30.643
Yes. So would some information.

00:15:30.851 --> 00:15:34.730
You went behind enemy lines. Come on,
the parents. What's the deal? Cyborgs?

00:15:34.938 --> 00:15:36.481
Supremacists? Vegans?

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.816
We went to his dad's dealership,
looked at cars.

00:15:39.025 --> 00:15:40.151
You guys friends now?

00:15:50.368 --> 00:15:52.536
First Summer and Anna.
Now you and Luke.

00:15:53.203 --> 00:15:55.372
They came out
of the bathroom together.

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:58.791
Then they went off
to the library together. Together.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.918
Stranger things have happened.

00:16:01.127 --> 00:16:05.088
Two people who hate each other,
brought together by their hatred of me.

00:16:05.297 --> 00:16:08.966
It's like Luke Skywalker and Darth Vader
teaming up to destroy the Emperor.

00:16:10.968 --> 00:16:14.513
- Hey, we should talk about...
- We got nothing to talk about.

00:16:14.721 --> 00:16:17.140
- Our presentation?
- I'll finish it myself.

00:16:17.348 --> 00:16:18.641
All right.

00:16:21.102 --> 00:16:24.354
- What are you looking at, queer?
- Somebody writing you new material?

00:16:24.563 --> 00:16:27.398
All right, go with what works.

00:16:28.399 --> 00:16:30.651
I... I gotta get to Spanish.

00:16:32.027 --> 00:16:36.573
So I guess this means you and Luke are
not friends, which I find oddly comforting.

00:16:37.949 --> 00:16:39.700
I promise.

00:17:02.261 --> 00:17:04.596
So, hey.

00:17:04.805 --> 00:17:05.806
That's a big test.

00:17:08.474 --> 00:17:10.309
You know what?

00:17:10.518 --> 00:17:11.685
Don't.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.655
Hey, wanna...? Over there?

00:17:25.822 --> 00:17:26.990
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:17:27.198 --> 00:17:29.283
- Is this seat taken?
- It is now.

00:17:29.492 --> 00:17:30.951
Cool.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:33.912
- So did you study for the bio thing?
- Kind of.

00:17:34.121 --> 00:17:35.288
Well, I didn't.

00:17:35.497 --> 00:17:37.373
Don't worry. All you have to remember is:

00:17:37.582 --> 00:17:40.334
Kittens prefer cream or fish,
generally speaking.

00:17:40.501 --> 00:17:41.877
Excuse me?

00:17:42.044 --> 00:17:45.672
Kingdom. Phylum. Class. Order.
Family. Genus. Species.

00:17:45.881 --> 00:17:48.716
- You're, like, really smart.
- Compared to what?

00:17:49.842 --> 00:17:51.093
Well, me.

00:17:52.177 --> 00:17:55.931
- Summer, you're smart.
- Well, smart enough to sit next to you.

00:17:56.139 --> 00:17:57.891
What was that kitten thing again?

00:17:58.099 --> 00:18:00.476
Kittens prefer cream or fish,
generally speaking.

00:18:00.685 --> 00:18:02.478
Or, if you're not a cat person:

00:18:02.686 --> 00:18:04.896
King Philip comes over for good sex.

00:18:05.105 --> 00:18:07.690
- Definitely not a cat person.
- Right.

00:18:07.899 --> 00:18:09.734
That's really good. Thanks.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.871
I am so sore. Are you?

00:18:25.163 --> 00:18:28.791
I'm fine. You must not
have stretched properly.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.128
Are you okay?

00:18:33.795 --> 00:18:36.172
Sandy told me about the house.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.804
Nothing to tell. I'm not selling.

00:18:44.012 --> 00:18:45.555
Julie...

00:18:46.306 --> 00:18:47.765
Julie.

00:18:48.975 --> 00:18:51.143
If you and Kaitlin
need somewhere to live...

00:18:51.352 --> 00:18:53.103
...I can find you a house.

00:18:53.312 --> 00:18:55.230
My dad can find you a house.

00:18:55.439 --> 00:18:59.150
Not according to him. Not without
compromising our relationship.

00:18:59.358 --> 00:19:00.568
He said that?

00:19:00.776 --> 00:19:04.780
So I told him if that's true, we don't have
to have a relationship. So now we don't.

00:19:04.988 --> 00:19:07.282
I had no idea. I'm so sorry.

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:10.743
Wow. You'd think you'd be celebrating.

00:19:10.951 --> 00:19:13.620
Go ahead. Tell everybody
that Caleb Nichol dumped me...

00:19:13.787 --> 00:19:16.706
...my husband's going to jail,
and I have no place to live.

00:19:16.915 --> 00:19:20.626
What you waiting for? I told them about
Thanksgiving. Now you can get even.

00:19:20.835 --> 00:19:22.419
If you need anything, let me know.

00:19:24.004 --> 00:19:29.092
Oh, my God! You guys, I just ran
into Betsy on the elliptical trainer.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:32.261
She was getting her car
serviced this morning.

00:19:32.469 --> 00:19:33.804
Okay, come here.

00:19:35.013 --> 00:19:37.432
Okay, you can't tell anyone...

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:42.102
...but you are not going
to believe this. Okay...

00:19:43.145 --> 00:19:46.273
I've never seen you hit the ball
like that, Jimmy. You crushed it.

00:19:46.523 --> 00:19:49.192
Creative visualization.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.944
- Julie's head.
- Get a realtor, show the house.

00:19:52.444 --> 00:19:54.613
- But she...
- Julie will change her tune.

00:19:55.238 --> 00:19:58.324
Once word spreads that the SEC
is investigating her...

00:19:58.533 --> 00:20:01.660
...as a possible co-conspirator,
forget about it.

00:20:01.869 --> 00:20:03.328
They are?

00:20:03.537 --> 00:20:05.288
I can make a call.

00:20:06.289 --> 00:20:07.749
Thank you.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.045
- I'll get this one.
- Thanks.

00:20:13.253 --> 00:20:17.298
You know, I gotta say,
you've just been incredibly...

00:20:17.465 --> 00:20:19.550
...cool with me. I...

00:20:19.759 --> 00:20:21.594
You know, considering...

00:20:21.802 --> 00:20:22.970
...everything.

00:20:23.554 --> 00:20:27.015
You know, I really appreciate, you know,
you just not saying anything...

00:20:27.223 --> 00:20:30.434
...and I know you only heard it
from Kirsten's point of view...

00:20:30.643 --> 00:20:32.561
...but I want you to hear it from me.

00:20:33.937 --> 00:20:38.191
That whole thing was just a huge mistake.
I'm really sorry.

00:20:38.399 --> 00:20:40.943
Jimmy, what the hell
are you talking about?

00:20:41.152 --> 00:20:44.446
- Kirsten didn't tell you?
- Tell me what?

00:20:53.412 --> 00:20:56.581
You know, when Julie kicked me out...

00:20:57.207 --> 00:21:00.084
...I was lost, and Kirsten...

00:21:00.293 --> 00:21:03.128
...came over to help me
set up my place.

00:21:03.795 --> 00:21:05.338
And...

00:21:08.132 --> 00:21:09.258
...I...

00:21:11.719 --> 00:21:13.262
...kissed her.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:18.933
Now, she was totally mortified. I...
And I apologized immediately.

00:21:19.434 --> 00:21:21.227
She left, like...

00:21:21.435 --> 00:21:22.895
...faster than that. I mean...

00:21:23.062 --> 00:21:26.731
And she didn't tell you, because she
didn't... She didn't want to hurt you.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:29.901
It meant nothing. So she didn't
want to hurt you over...

00:21:30.109 --> 00:21:31.735
Over nothing.

00:21:32.111 --> 00:21:35.405
Which now...

00:21:35.822 --> 00:21:37.615
...I've done.

00:21:38.783 --> 00:21:41.744
Creative visualization, Jimmy.

00:21:42.828 --> 00:21:45.747
I'm trying hard not to see your head
as something I should hit.

00:21:45.956 --> 00:21:47.665
Look, I'm really sorry.

00:21:47.874 --> 00:21:51.752
I, you know... I just didn't want there
to be any secrets between us.

00:21:54.755 --> 00:21:56.589
Mission accomplished.

00:22:01.969 --> 00:22:06.556
- Hey.
- I've some news, but I'm only telling you.

00:22:06.973 --> 00:22:10.101
Oh, my God.
Coop, you are not going to believe this.

00:22:10.309 --> 00:22:12.728
Did you hear about Luke's dad?

00:22:14.438 --> 00:22:15.939
I haven't heard about Luke's dad.

00:22:17.857 --> 00:22:21.735
- Hey, I have crazy news for you.
- It's about your woman problems.

00:22:21.944 --> 00:22:23.529
No, it's definitely not.

00:22:23.737 --> 00:22:26.197
I heard his dad's favorite show
is Dawson 's Crack.

00:22:26.406 --> 00:22:28.908
I heard it was Ever-woody.

00:22:29.117 --> 00:22:30.576
Wait, Ryan.

00:22:31.619 --> 00:22:34.079
- Hey, man, look...
- Who'd you tell?

00:22:34.288 --> 00:22:36.289
Listen, I'm sorry.

00:22:38.124 --> 00:22:39.667
You're dead.

00:22:49.801 --> 00:22:52.303
- Everyone knows.
- Yeah, well, who'd you tell?

00:22:52.386 --> 00:22:54.263
What? I didn't tell any...

00:22:54.304 --> 00:22:57.557
- Was it Summer? I asked you not to...
- Why do you just assume it was me?

00:22:57.765 --> 00:23:01.060
Because I'm the only one who knew,
and you're the only one I told.

00:23:06.523 --> 00:23:09.400
I didn't tell anyone.

00:23:09.484 --> 00:23:12.069
I never should've told you
in the first place.

00:23:12.152 --> 00:23:15.739
Probably not, since obviously
you don't trust me.

00:23:22.161 --> 00:23:25.080
You know what,
find your own ride home.

00:23:36.840 --> 00:23:38.466
Hey.

00:23:38.675 --> 00:23:40.134
Hey.

00:23:40.301 --> 00:23:45.263
It's amazing about the Wards.
How fast word travels.

00:23:45.472 --> 00:23:47.307
Sometimes.

00:23:48.474 --> 00:23:50.601
- I'd ask you if everything's okay...
- It's not.

00:23:51.143 --> 00:23:52.978
Which leads me to my next question.

00:23:53.187 --> 00:23:56.523
It's well-covered territory with us.

00:23:57.607 --> 00:23:59.484
Jimmy Cooper.

00:24:02.528 --> 00:24:07.407
I... I want to do my best
not to sound too...

00:24:07.782 --> 00:24:10.951
...high-school, but...

00:24:13.787 --> 00:24:15.580
He kissed you.

00:24:16.581 --> 00:24:18.041
He told you?

00:24:18.249 --> 00:24:21.419
He didn't want there to be any secrets
between us. Apparently...

00:24:21.627 --> 00:24:24.004
...you don't feel the same way.
- Of course I do.

00:24:24.213 --> 00:24:26.006
It's just that it meant nothing.

00:24:28.466 --> 00:24:31.886
Putting my own skepticism about
that remark aside for just a moment...

00:24:32.094 --> 00:24:33.762
...if it meant nothing...

00:24:34.888 --> 00:24:37.140
...then why didn't you tell me?

00:24:39.225 --> 00:24:41.769
- Because I knew it would upset you.
- Thank you.

00:24:41.977 --> 00:24:45.605
Because I feel much so better
having heard it from someone else.

00:24:46.815 --> 00:24:48.399
- I'm sorry.
- All this time...

00:24:48.608 --> 00:24:53.070
...this suspicion and paranoia
about me and my co-worker...

00:24:53.278 --> 00:24:56.031
...and you're sitting on this.
- Sandy...

00:24:56.197 --> 00:24:57.782
Sandy...

00:25:02.161 --> 00:25:04.830
It means nothing.

00:25:06.456 --> 00:25:09.333
It means something to me.

00:25:19.050 --> 00:25:23.720
Okay, it's just that, after all
the years of Luke calling me gay...

00:25:24.471 --> 00:25:26.556
...it's great that the shoe's on the other...

00:25:26.765 --> 00:25:29.475
Actually, it's on his dad's foot,
but you get the symmetry.

00:25:29.684 --> 00:25:31.435
It's not funny.

00:25:31.644 --> 00:25:34.646
It's the end of their marriage.
The life they knew is over.

00:25:34.855 --> 00:25:37.774
- I heard Meredith's filing for divorce.
- I was over there.

00:25:37.982 --> 00:25:40.359
- They seemed really happy.
- Yeah?

00:25:40.568 --> 00:25:42.861
By "happy," do you mean gay?

00:25:43.070 --> 00:25:44.905
Seth, cut it out.

00:25:45.113 --> 00:25:48.783
I mean, how can you be married for
that long and keep that kind of a secret?

00:25:48.991 --> 00:25:50.451
You'd be surprised.

00:25:50.660 --> 00:25:52.286
But eventually the secrets come out.

00:25:52.953 --> 00:25:56.331
And some marriages can handle
the truth, and some can't.

00:26:00.918 --> 00:26:03.754
Yeah, well, I'm sure everyone
will be so accepting...

00:26:03.962 --> 00:26:06.923
...seeing as we're
such a liberal, tolerant bunch.

00:26:07.132 --> 00:26:09.842
That was at the expense
of Orange County, not Luke's dad.

00:26:10.051 --> 00:26:12.177
His big gay dad.

00:26:12.386 --> 00:26:15.097
Did you see his arms?
What straight guy has arms like that?

00:26:15.305 --> 00:26:16.431
Not my husband.

00:26:16.640 --> 00:26:20.851
Charles and I went to see The Lion King
with the Wards, and Carson cried.

00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:22.478
Wept.

00:26:25.272 --> 00:26:29.067
All these years I've known him,
he's never once made a pass at me.

00:26:29.275 --> 00:26:31.735
I feel so much better.

00:26:34.488 --> 00:26:37.407
- I can't be here right now.
- Have you eaten?

00:26:37.615 --> 00:26:39.409
- What do you have in mind?
- Fried food and beer.

00:26:39.617 --> 00:26:41.285
First round's on me.

00:26:48.750 --> 00:26:53.504
All right, if everyone will take
his or her seat, we shall begin.

00:26:53.712 --> 00:26:56.256
Anyone seen Luke?

00:26:57.549 --> 00:27:00.092
Okay, let's open our books to page 59...

00:27:00.301 --> 00:27:03.345
...the Chesapeake
and the West Indian colonies.

00:27:04.930 --> 00:27:06.973
So you should come over, like, at 4.

00:27:07.182 --> 00:27:10.393
Yeah. I've got lit mag after school,
but I can come by after that.

00:27:10.601 --> 00:27:13.270
Okay, yeah, the flash cards
should be done by then.

00:27:14.730 --> 00:27:17.273
Hi, you guys.
Can I speak to you for one minute, please?

00:27:17.482 --> 00:27:20.526
Because I owe you both
an enormous apology.

00:27:21.610 --> 00:27:23.695
I guess, technically,
I owe two apologies...

00:27:23.904 --> 00:27:27.740
...each one tailored to the specific wrongs
visited upon the specific person.

00:27:27.949 --> 00:27:30.117
But since you two seem to be
a package deal...

00:27:30.326 --> 00:27:33.954
- Cohen!
- Right. I'm sorry. And I'm sorry.

00:27:34.162 --> 00:27:38.249
And I'm also sorry that I apologized
to her first. It's just, chronologically, l...

00:27:38.458 --> 00:27:39.876
- Cohen.
- Right. Stupid, I know.

00:27:40.084 --> 00:27:42.836
Well, let me start by saying
nothing in my life...

00:27:43.045 --> 00:27:47.549
...nothing, prepared me for the events
of that fateful Thanksgiving day.

00:27:47.757 --> 00:27:50.718
But I'm not gonna make
any excuses for what I did.

00:27:51.552 --> 00:27:54.054
I just wanna say one thing
in my defense, which is:

00:27:54.263 --> 00:27:57.891
You can't really blame me for wanting
the company of either of you two.

00:27:58.891 --> 00:28:02.061
And I know that I hurt your feelings
and I feel bad about that.

00:28:02.269 --> 00:28:06.690
I do, but please believe me when I say
that it wasn't intentional, okay?

00:28:06.898 --> 00:28:09.192
I would never do anything
to ruin our friendship...

00:28:09.400 --> 00:28:11.986
...or "-ships."

00:28:13.946 --> 00:28:15.572
I know I have no right to ask...

00:28:15.780 --> 00:28:18.783
...I just hope that some day
you can both forgive me.

00:28:22.119 --> 00:28:25.330
Okay. So, yeah, thanks for your time.

00:28:31.627 --> 00:28:34.713
You know, I never liked flash cards.
They never worked for me.

00:28:34.921 --> 00:28:37.215
Yeah, you know,
I think I study better alone.

00:28:37.424 --> 00:28:40.176
That's good, because I think
lit mag is going to go late.

00:28:40.384 --> 00:28:42.344
- Maybe next test?
- Maybe.

00:28:42.928 --> 00:28:45.013
It's like they enjoy it.

00:28:45.931 --> 00:28:49.392
Well, I can't exactly claim that I didn't
once see the fun in witnessing...

00:28:49.600 --> 00:28:52.353
...the fall of the rich and fabulous.

00:28:52.561 --> 00:28:55.897
Then I became homeless,
and suddenly not so funny.

00:28:56.106 --> 00:28:58.858
I don't really think that my dad
would let you go homeless.

00:28:59.067 --> 00:29:00.860
Yeah, well, when I even mentioned...

00:29:01.068 --> 00:29:03.821
...that I might have to sell
the house, he went into a panic.

00:29:04.154 --> 00:29:06.114
You'd have thought
I was asking for a ring.

00:29:06.323 --> 00:29:08.408
- That's so him.
- And when I tried to explain...

00:29:08.574 --> 00:29:10.159
- He didn't listen.
- Not a word.

00:29:10.368 --> 00:29:13.787
Can I ask you a question?
Do you like that he calls you Kiki?

00:29:13.996 --> 00:29:15.872
- Hate it.
- He kept calling me Juju...

00:29:16.081 --> 00:29:19.042
...like that candy that gets in your teeth.
I begged him to stop.

00:29:19.250 --> 00:29:21.919
- When he gets something in his head...
- It has to be his way.

00:29:22.086 --> 00:29:23.545
Always.

00:29:27.465 --> 00:29:29.175
It's just who he is.

00:29:29.967 --> 00:29:33.512
He can't spend longer than three months
with the same woman before he freaks.

00:29:33.720 --> 00:29:35.138
He freaked, all right.

00:29:35.347 --> 00:29:37.891
And I wish I could tell him
that I know what he's doing.

00:29:38.099 --> 00:29:40.768
He's trying to replace my mom.

00:29:40.935 --> 00:29:42.811
But he can't.

00:29:43.020 --> 00:29:47.398
And I just wish that he would
stop trying and be happy.

00:29:47.607 --> 00:29:50.401
- But you can't talk to my dad.
- No, I know.

00:29:51.652 --> 00:29:54.988
And the important thing is that he finds
someone to share his life with.

00:29:55.197 --> 00:29:57.449
Enjoy these years.

00:29:58.491 --> 00:30:01.494
I just don't know
if he's ever gonna figure that out.

00:30:13.712 --> 00:30:15.714
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:30:17.424 --> 00:30:19.634
So that apology...

00:30:19.842 --> 00:30:23.220
...aside from being the first
I've ever received from a boy...

00:30:23.429 --> 00:30:26.139
...was also the nicest.

00:30:26.348 --> 00:30:28.516
Well. Well...

00:30:28.725 --> 00:30:30.643
...I meant it, so, good.

00:30:35.647 --> 00:30:38.650
So, what are you doing Saturday?

00:30:45.155 --> 00:30:47.490
- Hey, Seth.
- Hey.

00:30:47.699 --> 00:30:49.784
- You going to lit mag?
- Yeah.

00:30:49.992 --> 00:30:51.994
Wanna walk together?

00:30:52.745 --> 00:30:54.830
- Do you?
- Yes.

00:30:55.038 --> 00:30:56.915
That was so sweet,
what you said earlier.

00:30:57.123 --> 00:30:59.000
And I could tell you really meant it.

00:30:59.208 --> 00:31:01.043
We know sincerity
isn't your strong point.

00:31:01.252 --> 00:31:04.504
- I'm working on it.
- I'd like to help.

00:31:06.423 --> 00:31:07.966
What are you doing Saturday night?

00:31:12.094 --> 00:31:15.180
Well, in the new spirit of sincerity...

00:31:16.890 --> 00:31:18.599
...I have a date with Summer.

00:31:20.893 --> 00:31:22.519
Yeah, so...

00:31:23.812 --> 00:31:25.439
What are you doing Friday night?

00:31:30.359 --> 00:31:32.820
What am I doing Friday night?

00:31:36.906 --> 00:31:40.076
- Hi. Why are you here?
- Same reason you are.

00:31:41.494 --> 00:31:43.120
- Hey.
- You okay, man?

00:31:59.383 --> 00:32:01.177
Look, man...

00:32:02.136 --> 00:32:04.096
I owe you an apology.

00:32:04.304 --> 00:32:05.722
It wasn't you who said anything.

00:32:05.931 --> 00:32:11.852
My dad, after we saw him,
he came out to my mom.

00:32:12.061 --> 00:32:18.024
She wigged and called a couple friends,
and then everybody in Newport knew.

00:32:18.233 --> 00:32:20.151
Don't worry about it. I just...

00:32:20.359 --> 00:32:22.820
...wanted to see how you were doing.

00:32:24.029 --> 00:32:25.655
Hey, Mom.

00:32:27.740 --> 00:32:29.283
Meredith, please.

00:32:32.578 --> 00:32:34.871
Luke, could I...?

00:32:35.080 --> 00:32:36.414
Luke, please.

00:32:42.878 --> 00:32:46.548
My entire life has been one giant lie.

00:32:48.633 --> 00:32:51.385
Everything I thought
I knew about my dad.

00:32:54.638 --> 00:32:57.390
I mean, all those business trips he took.

00:32:58.516 --> 00:33:02.436
Or how about when he missed one of my
games because he was working late.

00:33:03.520 --> 00:33:07.816
I don't even know if this guy was
the first one or if there were others.

00:33:09.233 --> 00:33:13.195
- I can't even think about it.
- Look, I know it's hard.

00:33:13.737 --> 00:33:18.074
But after everything I've been through
with my dad, we've never been closer.

00:33:18.283 --> 00:33:21.869
I mean, we're finally able to be honest
with each other and talk to each other.

00:33:22.077 --> 00:33:24.121
Maybe you could have that
with your dad.

00:33:24.329 --> 00:33:27.290
What he has to say, I don't wanna hear.

00:33:31.919 --> 00:33:35.338
I'm gonna go grab a jacket. It's cold.

00:33:37.173 --> 00:33:41.052
Well, even if he...

00:33:41.260 --> 00:33:43.929
...wasn't honest with you...

00:33:44.096 --> 00:33:45.180
...he still cared.

00:33:45.680 --> 00:33:47.515
He did make it
to some of your games.

00:33:47.724 --> 00:33:48.850
Whatever.

00:33:49.058 --> 00:33:50.935
What does it even matter?

00:33:51.560 --> 00:33:53.562
It matters.

00:33:54.730 --> 00:33:57.941
Especially if you had a dad who didn't
make it to any of your games.

00:33:58.149 --> 00:34:02.069
Who didn't even know
what sport you played or cared.

00:34:09.867 --> 00:34:12.828
Everything is just so screwed up.

00:34:14.496 --> 00:34:18.958
Isn't this romantic?
A couple of Harbor Butt Pirates.

00:34:19.542 --> 00:34:21.293
Is there a problem?

00:34:21.502 --> 00:34:23.921
Other than the fact
that we kick your ass every year?

00:34:24.129 --> 00:34:26.673
No, dude. No problem at all.

00:34:26.881 --> 00:34:28.508
Didn't mean to interrupt your date.

00:34:31.510 --> 00:34:33.554
Fag.

00:34:33.762 --> 00:34:36.056
What did you call me?

00:34:39.183 --> 00:34:41.185
Yo, dude, save that for your boyfriend.

00:34:41.393 --> 00:34:44.813
- Okay, let's just not do this.
- How about a black eye for the queer guy?

00:34:45.022 --> 00:34:47.398
Why don't you just run to your daddy.

00:35:03.037 --> 00:35:04.413
Julie, hi.

00:35:04.621 --> 00:35:07.040
I just had to come over
and say thank you.

00:35:07.207 --> 00:35:08.583
- For what?
- I got home today.

00:35:08.750 --> 00:35:11.961
There was a message on my machine,
"It's Caleb, call me." Whatever.

00:35:12.169 --> 00:35:14.379
- Well...
- I know. But I call him, right?

00:35:14.588 --> 00:35:18.174
Just in case he's ready to apologize,
which, P.S., he's not.

00:35:18.341 --> 00:35:21.385
So he starts again with the excuses,
and he's feeling pressured.

00:35:21.594 --> 00:35:23.720
- Well, because it's all about him.
- Exactly.

00:35:23.887 --> 00:35:27.223
But then I remembered what you said
at lunch, so I let him have it.

00:35:27.432 --> 00:35:29.767
- You did?
- I told him he's scared. Life's too short.

00:35:29.976 --> 00:35:32.936
- Spend it with someone you enjoy.
- You did?

00:35:33.145 --> 00:35:35.689
Don't worry, he doesn't think
it came from you.

00:35:35.897 --> 00:35:38.858
But the important thing is, it worked.

00:35:39.317 --> 00:35:41.777
- How so?
- Kirsten...

00:35:41.986 --> 00:35:45.072
...he's buying my house
as an investment.

00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:48.074
Jimmy's not going to jail.
Kaitlin and I have a place to live.

00:35:48.491 --> 00:35:49.742
And who knows...

00:35:49.909 --> 00:35:53.245
...maybe some day your
next-door neighbor will be your dad.

00:35:55.163 --> 00:35:57.082
I don't know what to say.

00:35:57.290 --> 00:36:00.459
Well, you might want to water that.
Bye.

00:36:14.263 --> 00:36:16.723
Here, you look like a strong, healthy boy.

00:36:16.890 --> 00:36:18.224
Give me a hand.

00:36:21.018 --> 00:36:22.895
Hey, Seth.

00:36:23.062 --> 00:36:25.397
Ask your mother who was at the door.

00:36:28.274 --> 00:36:30.735
Mom, who was at the door?

00:36:30.901 --> 00:36:34.404
- Julie Cooper, bearing gifts.
- Julie Cooper, Dad.

00:36:35.572 --> 00:36:37.574
Ask your mother what she wanted.

00:36:41.077 --> 00:36:42.911
Dad wants to know who...
What she wanted.

00:36:43.078 --> 00:36:46.581
Dad, better idea, ask her yourself.
Come on.

00:36:48.750 --> 00:36:51.210
Julie Cooper sold her house.

00:36:52.336 --> 00:36:54.338
To my father.

00:36:55.422 --> 00:36:57.715
Now that I wish you hadn't told me.

00:36:57.882 --> 00:37:00.176
- Hey.
- Oh, my God.

00:37:00.760 --> 00:37:02.177
Are you guys okay?

00:37:02.344 --> 00:37:05.639
- I didn't do it this time.
- I'm gonna get the first-aid kit.

00:37:05.847 --> 00:37:07.265
Come on, have a seat.

00:37:07.474 --> 00:37:09.559
Hey, what happened?

00:37:11.769 --> 00:37:13.562
I guess bad news travels fast.

00:37:13.770 --> 00:37:15.439
- Have you called your folks?
- No.

00:37:15.605 --> 00:37:18.650
- I'll call them.
- No. I'd rather not call them, if it's okay.

00:37:18.858 --> 00:37:22.278
- All right. He can stay in the guest room.
- Sure.

00:37:26.364 --> 00:37:29.117
- I'm gonna call his dad.
- Okay.

00:37:37.207 --> 00:37:40.876
So do you guys need
a ride to school in the morning?

00:37:41.043 --> 00:37:42.503
You don't mind?

00:37:42.711 --> 00:37:45.338
Yeah, well, you were pretty great
with Luke today.

00:37:45.589 --> 00:37:48.841
- I never should've told you.
- Because I'll tell everyone, right?

00:37:49.050 --> 00:37:52.594
- No, because he asked me not to.
- But the unwritten rule of relationships...

00:37:52.761 --> 00:37:55.055
...says you're allowed
to tell your girlfriend.

00:37:55.222 --> 00:37:59.225
Because everything you say to me
stays with me, and vice versa.

00:37:59.434 --> 00:38:03.270
So you didn't tell anybody I went off on
you yesterday when I thought you'd told?

00:38:03.479 --> 00:38:06.564
No. Well, I mean, just Summer.

00:38:09.442 --> 00:38:11.569
Will you tell Summer about this?

00:38:14.321 --> 00:38:17.323
No, this will stay just between us.

00:38:31.419 --> 00:38:34.338
Carson, are you sure
I can't get you anything to eat?

00:38:34.504 --> 00:38:36.589
Some Scotch? Xanax?

00:38:36.756 --> 00:38:38.883
No, thank you.

00:38:39.050 --> 00:38:41.218
- He's not coming down.
- Well, he's half-asleep.

00:38:41.427 --> 00:38:43.679
Maybe it'd be better
to talk in the morning.

00:38:43.887 --> 00:38:47.891
He's not gonna want to talk to me.
I lied to him.

00:38:48.433 --> 00:38:50.393
I lied to everyone. I...

00:38:52.686 --> 00:38:55.772
The truth is, I love his mom.
I always have.

00:38:55.981 --> 00:39:01.193
And I love our family.
And I just didn't want to hurt anybody.

00:39:01.735 --> 00:39:05.697
- And now he's up there hurting.
- Hey, if there's anything we can do...

00:39:05.906 --> 00:39:08.866
No. No, I've embarrassed
my family enough.

00:39:09.033 --> 00:39:11.744
I think the best thing
I could do now is to disappear.

00:39:11.911 --> 00:39:15.205
No, I think that'd be the worst
thing you could do. I mean...

00:39:15.414 --> 00:39:17.415
...it's what you've been doing all along.

00:39:17.624 --> 00:39:21.669
But coming out and being honest with
yourself and your family, in this town...

00:39:21.877 --> 00:39:23.879
...it's the bravest thing
you could've done.

00:39:24.046 --> 00:39:26.589
Look, it's just my opinion...

00:39:26.756 --> 00:39:29.967
...but you're the kind of father
any kid would be proud of.

00:39:31.052 --> 00:39:33.470
Well, I should go.

00:39:33.720 --> 00:39:35.472
Dad.

00:39:45.730 --> 00:39:47.690
Just let me grab my shoes.

00:39:49.358 --> 00:39:50.568
I'll go with you.

00:40:11.585 --> 00:40:14.463
So while we're being honest...

00:40:14.630 --> 00:40:16.339
Oh, God.

00:40:16.548 --> 00:40:18.341
There's more?

00:40:18.591 --> 00:40:21.177
That was a pretty impressive speech
you made in there.

00:40:21.343 --> 00:40:23.178
Well, I'm prone to impressive speeches.

00:40:23.345 --> 00:40:25.472
Right up until that line, yeah.

00:40:27.140 --> 00:40:30.476
- From now on, you'll tell all your secrets?
- You gonna tell me all yours?

00:40:30.643 --> 00:40:32.686
- You know, I don't think I have any.
- Really?

00:40:32.895 --> 00:40:34.104
- Yeah.
- You sure?

00:40:34.313 --> 00:40:36.523
- I think.
- Nothing from your past?

00:40:36.731 --> 00:40:38.775
No secret fantasies?

00:40:38.983 --> 00:40:41.986
No hidden porn stash on the PC?

00:40:42.194 --> 00:40:44.696
No, because obviously you
already know about that one.

00:40:49.909 --> 00:40:55.372
There's no way you can know
everything about someone.

00:40:55.580 --> 00:41:00.001
- That's what keeps it interesting.
- Well, it hasn't been uninteresting.

00:41:00.167 --> 00:41:03.170
At a certain point,
you have to trust the other person.

00:41:03.337 --> 00:41:06.214
- That's what love is.
- Okay.

00:41:06.423 --> 00:41:11.343
So you'll have to trust that you can
tell me things that I may not wanna hear.

00:41:11.635 --> 00:41:14.012
We can handle it.

00:41:16.014 --> 00:41:17.515
Like...

00:41:18.266 --> 00:41:20.226
...Jimmy Cooper kissed me?

00:41:23.479 --> 00:41:25.313
Trust me.

00:41:46.164 --> 00:41:49.042
- This is gonna be weird.
- Yep.

00:41:49.208 --> 00:41:52.503
Everybody's gonna be
staring at me and talking.

00:41:52.711 --> 00:41:54.004
Yep.

00:42:00.551 --> 00:42:02.845
Maybe I can just blow
the whole thing off...

00:42:03.053 --> 00:42:06.348
...go hit the beach, give everybody time
to get it out of their systems.

00:42:06.556 --> 00:42:10.017
It doesn't work like that. It's been
months. I'm still the kid from Chino...

00:42:10.184 --> 00:42:11.477
...that burned a house down.

00:42:11.644 --> 00:42:14.688
And I'm still the girl
who tried to kill herself in Mexico.

00:42:14.896 --> 00:42:17.023
And I'm still the...

00:42:17.190 --> 00:42:18.650
I'm still Seth Cohen.

00:42:20.318 --> 00:42:22.027
Man, this is gonna suck.

00:42:22.194 --> 00:42:25.322
Yep. Well, welcome to my world.
